'''Creighton's slender opossum''' ('''''Marmosops creightoni'''''), also known commonly as '''Voss' slender opossum'''<ref name = "Beolens"/> is a species of [[South America]]n [[opossum]] of the family [[Didelphidae]]. It is known only from the valley of the [[Rio Zongo]] in [[La Paz Department, Bolivia]], where it lives in [[Andes|Andean]] [[cloud forest]]s at elevations between 1800 and 3000 m.<ref name="iucn status 19 November 2021" /> It was named after [[G. Ken Creighton]] by fellow American zoologist [[Robert S. Voss]].<ref name = "Beolens">{{Cite book
